{"Django's ORM does not support negative slice indices \u2014 queryset[negative:stop] raises AssertionError. This path will crash at runtime whenever a cursor with a negative offset is submitted. The comment claiming the underlying Django ORM properly handles negative slicing automatically is incorrect": 0.9778915643692017, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key calls math.floor(value) / math.ceil(value) directly on the attribute value. When used with order_by=\"-datetime\", getattr(item, \"datetime\") returns a datetime object, and math.floor(datetime_obj) raises TypeError. Needs datetime-to-float conversion like DateTimePaginator does": 0.9836127758026123, "organization_context.member is typed as RpcOrganizationMember | None and can be None (e.g., for superusers who are not members of the organization). Accessing .has_global_access on None will raise an AttributeError": 0.9091984629631042, "The max_segment_spans guard was removed from _load_segment_data, removing read-time span count enforcement. If max_segment_spans is still intended as a configurable safety limit, the check should be preserved; otherwise the parameter and its metric are now dead code": 0.9087629318237305}